# Payment Gateway – example requests (VS Code REST Client, Rider, Visual Studio).
# Local run: dotnet run --project src/PaymentGateway.Api (simulator: docker compose up -d bank_simulator)
# With Docker Compose use: @base = http://localhost:8090
@base = http://localhost:5067

### Authorized – the simulator authorizes cards ending in an odd digit
# @name processPayment
POST {{base}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248877",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 1050,
  "cvv": "123"
}

### Declined – cards ending in an even digit
POST {{base}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248878",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 1050,
  "cvv": "123"
}

### Rejected – 400 listing every invalid field; the bank is not called
POST {{base}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "1234",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "gbp",
  "amount": 0,
  "cvv": "123"
}

### Bank unavailable – 503 bank_unavailable (the simulator fails cards ending in 0)
POST {{base}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248870",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 1050,
  "cvv": "123"
}

### Retrieve – process-then-retrieve; body equals the processing response above
GET {{base}}/api/payments/{{processPayment.response.body.$.id}}

### Retrieve – not found: a well-formed but unissued id
GET {{base}}/api/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Retrieve – malformed id: matches no route, 404 without echoing the value
GET {{base}}/api/payments/abc

### Unknown route – 404 ProblemDetails with traceId
GET {{base}}/api/unknown

### Health – liveness
GET {{base}}/health
